# TLS-terminating reverse proxy in front of the whole stack (docs/
# DEPLOYMENT.md item 3, production-readiness-adjacent GCP deployment
# work). Chosen over nginx+certbot: automatic Let's Encrypt issuance,
# renewal, and HTTP->HTTPS redirect from this ~10 lines, no separate
# ACME-webroot volume/renewal cron/reload-hook to get right. Sits in
# front of the existing `ui` service (nginx, frontend/nginx.conf.template)
# unchanged - that config still owns serving the built frontend and
# proxying /api/ to `backend` internally; Caddy's only job is TLS.
#
# {$DOMAIN} is gated via docker-compose.prod.yml's own env var default
# (${DOMAIN-:80}) - a real domain here makes Caddy provision a genuine
# Let's Encrypt certificate automatically (Caddy's core "automatic
# HTTPS" behavior needs no extra directives for this); left unset, it
# falls back to plain ":80" (any host, no TLS attempt) so the stack is
# still reachable and testable before DNS/a domain is ready - attempting
# ACME issuance against an IP address or no address at all would just
# fail loudly for no benefit during that phase.
{$DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy ui:80 {
		transport http {
			read_timeout 600s
			write_timeout 600s
		}
	}
}
